    "rawResponses": {
      "classes": "1: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a bank.\n2: NO MATCH -- An incident management team is not the general class of organizational units.\n3: NO MATCH -- An incident management team is not an IT operations team.\n4: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a service desk.\n5: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a network operations centre.\n6: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a security operations centre.\n7: NO MATCH -- An incident commander or approver is not a technical owner.\n8: NO MATCH -- An incident commander or approver is not a business owner.\n9: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a vendor.\n10: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a regulator.\n11: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a business process.\n12: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a service level objective.\n13: NO MATCH -- No candidate is an application.\n14: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a database.\n15: NO MATCH -- No candidate is an infrastructure component.\n16: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a server.\n17: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a virtual machine.\n18: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a container platform.\n19: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a cloud service.\n20: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a network device.\n21: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a network segment.\n22: NO MATCH -- No candidate is an endpoint.\n23: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a storage system.\n24: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a data centre.\n25: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a site.\n26: NO MATCH -- No candidate is an environment.\n27: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a data asset.\n28: NO MATCH -- No candidate is an integration interface.\n29: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a monitoring tool.\n30: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a monitoring rule.\n31: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a metric.\n32: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a log source.\n33: NO MATCH -- A communication about an incident is not an event in general.\n34: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a security event.\n35: NO MATCH -- An incident-response role or message is not a cybersecurity incident.\n36: NO MATCH -- No candidate is an emergency change.\n37: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a release.\n38: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a business continuity plan.\n39: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a disaster recovery test.\n40: NO MATCH -- Stakeholder communication is narrower than communication in general.\n41: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a post-incident review.",
      "relationships": "1: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a team coordinating a major incident.\n2: NO MATCH -- “Includes” a team is not membership in it.\n3: NO MATCH -- Requiring a commander is not being commanded by one.\n4: NO MATCH -- No candidate links backup sets to configuration items.\n5: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a recovery plan recovering a service.\n6: NO MATCH -- No candidate links alerts to IT services.\n7: NO MATCH -- No candidate links alerts to configuration items.\n8: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an incident impacting a business service.\n9: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an incident affecting a configuration item.\n10: NO MATCH -- No candidate links incidents to on-call engineers.\n11: NO MATCH -- Requiring a commander is not being coordinated by one.\n12: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes an incident notifying a stakeholder.\n13: NO MATCH -- Being linked to a change does not mean being resolved by it.\n14: NO MATCH -- The candidate gives a known error a corrective action, not a workaround.\n15: NO MATCH -- No candidate links known errors to configuration items.\n16: NO MATCH -- No candidate documents a workaround in a runbook.\n17: NO MATCH -- Implementing a deployment is not modifying a configuration item.\n18: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a change affecting an IT service.\n19: NO MATCH -- The candidate says a change implements a deployment, not a corrective action.\n20: NO MATCH -- No candidate links regulatory notifications to incidents.\n21: NO MATCH -- No candidate describes a regulatory notification including evidence.",
      "properties": "1: NO MATCH -- Declaration status is not the time the incident was declared.\n2: NO MATCH -- Status is not the diagnosed cause.\n3: NO MATCH -- Status is not a workaround summary.\n4: NO MATCH -- Neither candidate is the change summary.\n5: NO MATCH -- Neither candidate is the change’s risk level.\n6: NO MATCH -- Implementation time is not the planned start.\n7: NO MATCH -- Implementation time is not the planned end.\n8: NO MATCH -- Neither candidate is an implementation plan.\n9: NO MATCH -- Neither candidate is a backout plan.\n10: NO MATCH -- Plan status is not a recovery time objective.\n11: NO MATCH -- Plan status is not a recovery point objective.\n12: NO MATCH -- Plan status is not the last review date.",
